{
    "_doc_futureBases": "PLANNED: a dozen+ fixed-gender human bases, each with its own portrait handler. When they exist, for jp_generic_adult_male/female: (1) set targetBaseIDs to that gender's base list (one is picked at random; repeat an ID to weight it), (2) REMOVE Appearance, setHeight and setWeight - with Appearance unset the generator keeps each base's own gender, genital sizes, sensitivities and height/weight (setting it would reset them to gender defaults), while heightVariation/weightVariation still apply on top of the base's own size, (3) drop jp_generic_adult_base. Portraits need no generator work: the generated copy carries its base's Portrait, and BaseID stays the picked base (only baseTemplateID becomes the generator), so PortraitManager.ResetPortraits still resolves the right base. Role generators need no change. PARTIAL: female hospital staff already use this pattern via jp_hospital_doctor_female/jp_hospital_nurse_female (role-specific, so a doctor never gets a nurse portrait).",
    "_doc": "Generic modern-Japan NPC generators. jp_generic_adult_male/female randomize name (Japanese, family name first), stats and size, and roll sexual history (collections live in the nsfw file next to this one - in safe mode they are simply not found and skipped). Role generators (doctor/nurse/clerk) omit Appearance so they keep the gender of whichever generic generator they pick; the gender ratio is set by repeating IDs in targetBaseIDs. Roles are classified by the generator (title/baseTemplateID) only - no profession experience yet.",

